 ## Background
-This method is derived from implementations in Gaussian Splatting libraries, specifically those targeting Vulkan and WGPU backends [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. The explicit calculation of focal lengths and the handling of coordinate system conversions are adaptations for the specific requirements of splat shaders, which often operate in a different coordinate space than standard rasterization pipelines [S3, unofficial]. The use of `glm::lookAt` and `glm::perspective` is common in OpenGL-based implementations [S3, unofficial], while WGPU implementations may require additional matrix conversions [S2, unofficial].
